# D1a · Topology, normal behavior per Google: capacity-aware routing sends more writes where there is room (script_v2: B03).
# Pack draft (see CHANGELOG). SIMPLIFIED and GENERIC: Google does not publish GCS's internal topology.
# Google's report only says the optimization bypassed "the standard capacity-aware routing logic" and that the full revert
# restored "the previous capacity-aware routing behavior ... allowing traffic to distribute evenly across the region".
# Node count and arrow weights (thick = more writes, thin but not zero = less traffic) are illustrative (script_v2 B03).
# Text bands: labels KEY >= 36 px, x_* SECONDARY >= 28 px, foot SOURCE >= 22 px, at 1920x1080.
...@_style
...@_style_v05
vars: {d2-config: {pad: 24}}
grid-rows: 3
grid-gap: 30

title: "Google Cloud Storage · us-central1 · normal behavior" {
  shape: text
  style: {font: mono; font-color: "#E6EDF7"}
  x_sub: "simplified, based on Google's report" {shape: text; style: {font: mono; font-color: "#8C9EBF"}}
}

main: "" {
  style.opacity: 0
  grid-columns: 3
  grid-gap: 110
  side: "" {
    style.opacity: 0
    grid-rows: 2
    grid-gap: 20
    clients: "customers\nuploads ·\nWriteObject" {class: person; width: 240; height: 220}
    pad: "" {style.opacity: 0; width: 10; height: 40}
  }
  lb: "GCS load balancing layer" {
    class: boundary
    car: "standard\ncapacity-aware\nrouting logic" {class: ok; width: 400; height: 200}
  }
  nodes: "storage backend nodes" {
    class: boundary
    grid-rows: 2
    grid-gap: 60
    n1: "room available" {class: ok; width: 420; height: 140}
    s1: "low serving\ncapacity" {class: warn; width: 420; height: 140}
  }
  side.clients -> lb.car: "writes" {class: req}
  lb.car -> nodes.n1: "more writes" {class: req; style.stroke-width: 9}
  lb.car -> nodes.s1: "less traffic" {class: req; style.stroke-width: 2}
}

foot: "Google doesn't publish this topology or how the routing weighs capacity · node count and arrow weights are illustrative\nGoogle, on the full revert: \"restoring the previous capacity-aware routing behavior and allowing traffic to\ndistribute evenly across the region\" · incident report, 14 Oct 2026 · status.cloud.google.com/incidents/mSFVt6PiP557bjRyYsut" {class: note}

**.style.font-size: 36
**.style.bold: true
**.x_*.style.font-size: 28
**.x_*.style.bold: false
foot.style.font-size: 22
foot.style.bold: false
(** -> **)[*].style.font-size: 36
(** -> **)[*].style.bold: true
